{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1526169-what-if-ptc-gtse-btp-and-dtr-were-release-in-the-1990s","id":1526169,"title":"What if PtC, GTSE, BtP, and DtR were release in the 1990s?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-11-30T01:23:49-08:00","id":1526169,"title":"What if PtC, GTSE, BtP, and DtR were release in the 1990s?","content":"How would the book theme and mood change? How would it's influence the Meta-Plot of other gameline? And what kind of Meta-Plot would these game have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-30T05:11:58-08:00","id":1526175,"title":"","content":"I suspect Promethean would have been either a Mage or World of Darkness sourcebook about Constructs (WoD: The Created or something like that) with rules for playing homunculi, androids, clones, uplifted animals, patchwork people, and other beings created via Magic/Enlightened Science. <br /> <br /> Geist probably would have been an alteration to how Mediums work in Wraith.<br /> <br /> I'm not familiar enough with Beast or Deviant to guess about those.<br /> <br /> <br /> Tangentially, I have sometimes considered the idea of an alternate World of Darkness were you only had the original five games and the various WoD books (Sorcerer, Psychics, Mummy, etc.) that ran for about 13 years before ending with the Time of Judgement series, and then after that do an entirely new 21st century setting built around versions of Hunter the Reckoning, Mummy the Resurrection, Demon the Fallen, Promethean the Created, and maybe Deviant the Renegades. Call it A World of Fire or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-30T05:25:24-08:00","id":1526176,"title":"","content":"Beast would fit in pretty nicely into Changeling\u2019s lore as agents of the fomorian dream or playable fomorians. Instead of undergoing the changing way they devour their hosts soul and corrupt the dreaming by spreading their lairs, and players have the option to try and fight against their horror give in to it. Heroes probably wouldn\u2019t be needed, since WoD has options for that already and Changelings would be uniquely suited to battle them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-30T05:34:07-08:00","id":1526177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1526169-what-if-ptc-gtse-btp-and-dtr-were-release-in-the-1990s?p=1526175#post1526175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect Promethean would have been either a Mage or World of Darkness sourcebook about Constructs (WoD: The Created or something like that) with rules for playing homunculi, androids, clones, uplifted animals, patchwork people, and other beings created via Magic/Enlightened Science.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Promethean would have been a good fit right between Mage and Mummy. When the latter introduced mummies from other cultures, there would have been a place for artificial Undying imo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-30T05:56:22-08:00","id":1526181,"title":"","content":"I feel like Promethean is strong enough, and they really did a frankenstein game, that it could be its own game line. Also people arguing endlessly about if Mages and Vampires could make them is very WoD. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m not sure much would change though. Promethean\u2019s themes and mood fits very nicely into the WoD as is.<br /> <br /> I think Deviant fits better into Mage or a generic WoD crossover book. The focus is people taken by shadowy organizations and transformed via magic or science who are trying to understand what happened to them and get revenge. That fits so nicely into a not quite neutral faction in the ascension war, a rogue element punishing either side for using normal people as weapons while not fully understanding or caring about the bigger picture. The loyalist supplement would be rules for playing someone transformed that are fine with it, giving people who don\u2019t want to play a mage or whatever options to join those games.<br /> <br /> The core themes of Deviant would probably be the same, made a bit more edgy since you\u2019re a monster driven by revenge alienating people around you. Since CoD didn\u2019t have a ton of globe spanning conspiracies secretly pulling the strings of humanity Deviant had a ton of rules for building unique conspiracies that were creating deviants. I feel like that would go out the door in WoD and deviants would be tied to specific existing lore. If you made Deviant a book that wasn\u2019t tied to a specific game line then it would make the most sense to use the antagonist factions from each game as the source. Pentex (and maybe a new Weaver faction), Technocratic conventions, and the Sabbat (via flesh crafting).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-30T15:01:10-08:00","id":1526193,"title":"","content":"Being realistic I think the following would happen:<br /> <br /> The Prometheans would come in as a mage's expansion, a module on how to create familiars or something like that, if people really wanted it they would make a game based on that in later editions, then it depends on how the world-building would turn out and how they would develop the story of the Prometheans, I don't know how the theme of the story would work.<br /> <br /> Geist would be an expansion of the wraith involving mediums and a possible new NPC/Antagonist, if it was well accepted I think they would update the wraith to now be the sin-eaters making a rebbot of this part of the franchise, Wraith the Divided.<br /> <br /> The primordials would be changeling villains, perhaps with their own supplement, but I don't think they would come out of that.<br /> <br /> Deviant, I think it would be an expansion of WTA or something separate that they would try to position as a spin-off capable of being merged with other franchises.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-30T22:46:26-08:00","id":1526198,"title":"","content":"Fun fact: Constructed people called Prometheans are in the <b>Mage Storyteller's Handbook</b>, starting on p. 154. They don't have any specific powers or Disquiet (though they can be sorcerers if you want), but the book was developed by Bill Bridges, who I believe originally pitched <b>Promethean</b>, and did ultimately develop it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-01T09:49:07-08:00","id":1526203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1526169-what-if-ptc-gtse-btp-and-dtr-were-release-in-the-1990s?p=1526198#post1526198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fun fact: Constructed people called Prometheans are in the <b>Mage Storyteller's Handbook</b>, starting on p. 154. They don't have any specific powers or Disquiet (though they can be sorcerers if you want), but the book was developed by Bill Bridges, who I believe originally pitched <b>Promethean</b>, and did ultimately develop it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bridges wrote the original Sons of Ether tradition book, which included both an Awakened artificial being as one of its templates as well as an NPC who was essentially Frankenstein's monster (I'm sadly blanking on said character's name).<br /> <br /> The original draft of the STH's Promethean character creation guidelines included the possibility of them being Awakened (only having two dots in Spheres similar to Initiate characters IIRC), but that was cut from the final draft for whatever reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-01T11:57:40-08:00","id":1526205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1526169-what-if-ptc-gtse-btp-and-dtr-were-release-in-the-1990s?p=1526203#post1526203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bridges wrote the original Sons of Ether tradition book, which included both an Awakened artificial being as one of its templates as well as an NPC who was essentially Frankenstein's monster (I'm sadly blanking on said character's name).<br /> <br /> The original draft of the STH's Promethean character creation guidelines included the possibility of them being Awakened (only having two dots in Spheres similar to Initiate characters IIRC), but that was cut from the final draft for whatever reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>His name was Adam Waldman. I read about him in the original Society of Ether tradition book (except they were called Sons of Ether back then).<br /> <br /> Doc Eon (an early version of Maxwell Mercer from the Aeon Society?) was also in either the original or the revised SoE tradition book, I forget which.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":26996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","user":"Amethyst","date":". 12-01-2023, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-01T12:34:39-08:00","id":1526206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1526169-what-if-ptc-gtse-btp-and-dtr-were-release-in-the-1990s?p=1526205#post1526205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Doc Eon (an early version of Maxwell Mercer from the Aeon Society?) was also in either the original or the revised Size tradition book, I forget which.</div> </div> </div> </div>The original. He was Bill Bridges' creation, based on the 1930s pulp character Doc Savage.<br /> <br /> The other pulp era Tradition characters, based on Tarzan, Carnaki, The Shadow, The Phantom, Tin Tin, and others, were mentioned in Guide to the Traditions. The Technocracy ones were never named, but were supposed to be based on Operator 5, G-8, the Gladiator, Little Orphan Annie, and Flash Gordon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-03T11:44:22-08:00","id":1526282,"title":"","content":"I believe that Prometheans are also mentioned in <i>\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</i>the SoE section of <i>Lore of the Traditions.</i> Possibly the same one from the older material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}